WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.200
-With five weeks to go
until the midterms,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.934
Republicans are trying
to pretend

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.767
they have a serious
governing philosophy.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.801
But the leader of their party,
Donald Trump,

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.501
is making
that difficult for them

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.734
by claiming all elections
are now rigged

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:15.734
and launching a deranged attack
on Mitch McConnell and his wife,

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.934
Trump's former Transportation
secretary, Elaine Chao.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.534
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:24.067
♪♪

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.767
Even if you're someone who
follows politics very closely,

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.367
you'd be hard pressed to name
a single Republican policy idea,

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:32.934
aside from cutting rich people's
taxes or banning abortions,

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.601
or passing a law
that says it's illegal

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:39.767
to win an election if your name
is not Donald Trump Senior.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:43.033
Don't try to sneak in
on a technicality,

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.567
which is why Republicans
are now trying

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.033
to at least
create the appearance

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.634
that they have a plan to tackle
the issues people care about

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:52.167
by debuting what they're calling
a "Commitment to America."

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.534
House GOP leader
Kevin McCarthy

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.767
debuted the plan
at an event last month.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.234
Although if you ask me,
it looks like it might be light

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.567
on specifics
just from the size alone.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:01.734
-What we're going to roll
out today

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.667
is a Commitment to America,

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.601
and we want to roll it
out to you,

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:10.567
to the entire country,
to know exactly what we will do.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:13.868
If you would trust us
and give us the ability

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:16.167
to take a new direction
for this country,

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.934
what the commitment is,
is a plan.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.834
A plan for a new direction.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:23.334
So you know what?

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.667
We've created
a Commitment to America.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:29.200
-I think it's a bad sign
when your plan

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.601
for the future of the nation
can be pulled out of your pocket

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:34.901
like it's an acceptance speech
at the Emmys.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.601
"You want us to lead the nation?
Oh, my God,

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:38.300
This is such a surprise.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.167
First off,
I have to thank my agent

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.601
and all the good people
at A24 and, um..."

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:43.934
[ Fanfare plays ]
No! No!

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.300
They're playing me off.
Uh, thank you, uh, Fox News,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.100
my kids, Zachary and Tallulah.
Go to bed! [Kissing]"

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.567
Seriously? That's your plan?

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:57.334
The user manual for my
dishwasher is thicker than that.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:02:00.100
But I guess we can't be shocked
the GOP's plan to fix America

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.267
is the size of a poster
stapled to a telephone pole

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.701
that says "free guitar lessons"

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:06.634
when the guy who came up with it
is the same guy who once said

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.501
this at a Trump rally in 2020.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.701
-I want you to watch
Nancy Pelosi hand me that gavel.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:17.467
And I promise you this --

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.133
I won't bang her with it,

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:24.534
but I'll bang the end to the
socialism, and yes to America.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:31.868
-"I'll bang the end to the
socialism, and yes to America."

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:36.767
That sounds like a mad lib
filled out after a concussion.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:38.200
Did somebody bang you
with a gavel?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.634
Seriously, what does that mean?

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.434
That's like something
you'd see on a bootleg MAGA hat

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:44.834
you bought online
from a foreign country.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.801
Also, it's funny that
whenever these guys screw up,

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.434
they think they can save it
just by saying

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.400
"yes to America" at the end,
like it's the equivalent

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.434
of saying "San Dimas
High School football rules."

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:54.701
[ Siren wails ]

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:55.901
Oh!

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.701
It's an '80s reference
for old people.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.300
You know what that siren means?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.467
If you got that joke, it's time
to schedule your prostate exam,

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:09.033
because putting your health
first is always excellent

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.834
and waiting
until too late is...

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.367
-Both: Bogus.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:13.968
-Anyway...

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:19.234
The GOP's Commitment to America
has been so underwhelming

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:21.767
that even Fox News has been
questioning why it's so thin.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.300
The number three House
Republican, Elise Stefanik,

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.901
was asked that question
on Fox recently,

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:28.567
and unsurprisingly, she did not
have a very good answer.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:29.801
-Let's start
with this description

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.334
by New York magazine.
It says,

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:34.300
"The document has lots of bells
and whistles and factoids

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.868
about the hellish reign of Joe
Biden and his 'Democrat' Party.

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:40.167
What it doesn't have
is a whole lot of specificity."

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.267
You heard that
from the president,

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:42.334
from other Democrats, too,

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.868
who say
there are a lot of slogans.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.501
Yes, everybody wants
a safe country.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:48.434
They want good education.
They want crime to go down.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.501
But it's the details
of how you do that that matter.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:54.334
So why not more details
in this plan?

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.701
-Shannon, there are
ample details.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.100
So, number one,
an economy that's strong.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.367
-Son of a gun,
that is a good idea.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.467
Do they honestly expect voters
sitting at home

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:06.634
watching to hear that
and think, "Hmm, strong economy?

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.167
I like the sound of that."

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.601
It's like one of those
commercials where someone

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.801
at the kitchen table
responds to a bodiless voice

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.501
asking questions
about making your life better

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:16.200
without ever giving any answers
as to how.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.868
"Would you like to make
more money?"

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.334
Yes.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.701
"Would you like to do it from
the comfort of your own home?"

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:22.868
Sure.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:25.167
"Do you want a bigger house?
A nicer car?"

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.367
I do.

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:27.868
"Would you like to improve
your marriage

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.501
and spice up your sex life?"

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:32.334
Definitely.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:33.667
"Would you like to learn more?"

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.267
Uh, yes, please.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:40.567
"Then call
1-800-155-UHHHHHHHHHHHH."

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.133
They won't give up
on this dumb pamphlet.

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:43.534
They keep trying
to make it a thing.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:45.534
Even though Republicans
themselves are unenthused by it,

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:47.400
McCarthy and Stefanik
in particular

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.133
keep showing it off
and even trying to give it

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:50.400
to people as a gift.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.534
-Join us in supporting
the Commitment to America.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:56.133
A new direction.
Democrats have no plan.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:59.167
House Republicans have a plan,
and it's our commitment to you.

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:01.400
-Let's bring in House Minority
Leader Kevin McCarthy,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.767
who joins us here on the couch.
Sir, thanks for being here.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.033
-Thanks for having me.
-Great to have you.

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.934
-This is exactly
what we're talking about.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.467
I got a present
for all of you --

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.601
your own Commitment to America.

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:13.367
And in here,
we talk about a government

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:14.601
that's held accountable.

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:16.801
-You know, we've accused
Republicans of being

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:18.734
in a cult of personality
around Donald Trump,

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.868
and they're not helping
when they literally walk around

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.400
handing out pamphlets.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.934
But at least the Fox News hosts
looked super psyched about it.

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.634
That's the way your kid looks
when they're expecting

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:30.868
a PS5 for Christmas

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:32.667
and instead, you give him
a New York City T-shirt

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:35.434
you definitely
bought at the airport.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:37.467
In fact, I'm pretty sure
at the same time

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:39.400
Joe Biden was on "Morning Joe,"
giving each of the hosts

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.901
their their own PS5,
which makes sense.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.767
He's so desperate
to win back young voters.

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.334
I wouldn't be surprised
if he made a cameo

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:50.434
in season three of "Euphoria."
[As Biden] "Come on, guys.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:53.434
Let's stop with all this sex
and drugs and take the Amtrak

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:56.267
down to the swimming hole for
some good old-fashioned fun."

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:57.501
[ Siren wails ]

00:05:57.501 --> 00:05:59.367
[Normally] Oh, you know
what that siren means?

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:02.367
A modern reference
for young people.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:04.767
We did one for the olds,
and now one for you guys.

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:07.167
We are shamelessly pandering
to win over Gen Z.

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:09.434
And hey youngs, psst, over here.

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:12.067
I know I reference old movies,
but I like cool stuff.

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:14.234
Fezco and Rue?
That's my "Bill and Ted."

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:16.133
And if you love young stuff,
you'll love

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:20.434
"Late Night with Seth Meyers'"
hot new segment, A Closer Lewk.

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:21.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.067
[ Dance music plays ]

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:26.567
That music is way too loud.

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:31.934
♪♪

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:34.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:40.467
Also, I take it back.
That's not music.

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:49.801
Anyway, there's a reason this
dumb new pamphlet is so flimsy

00:06:49.801 --> 00:06:51.734
and why even GOP cheerleaders
on Fox News

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:53.367
are so unenthusiastic about it,
and that's because

00:06:53.367 --> 00:06:55.834
the GOP doesn't actually
have a discernible policy agenda

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.267
or a serious
governing philosophy.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:59.000
It's just a coalition
held together

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.334
by resentment and paranoia
and conspiracy theories

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:03.100
and culture war issues,
and above all else,

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.868
a hostility to democracy
that is still best embodied

00:07:05.868 --> 00:07:07.901
by their leader
and "People" magazine's

00:07:07.901 --> 00:07:10.868
Sweatiest Man Alive
for six years running,

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:13.601
Donald Trump. There's no
ideological core to the GOP

00:07:13.601 --> 00:07:15.467
that's distinct from Trumpism,
as Trump himself

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:18.000
demonstrated over the weekend
when he held a rally in Michigan

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.767
and once again whined
about the various investigations

00:07:20.767 --> 00:07:23.434
into his criminal behavior
while also denouncing

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:26.267
the legitimacy of all
future elections unless he wins.

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:29.000
And as usual, he also did it
in the weirdest way possible.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:33.400
-But I'm afraid we have never
had -- and I don't believe --

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.501
I don't believe we'll ever have
a fair election again.

00:07:37.501 --> 00:07:40.234
The way they win
is to cheat in elections.

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:43.367
They cheat like dogs.

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:45.901
Now...

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:47.934
Trump hates dogs.
That's indisputable.

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.601
But he really doesn't seem
to know what dogs do.

00:07:50.601 --> 00:07:54.067
I mean, they can pee on rugs,
they can chew up your shoes.

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:57.434
But in what way do dogs cheat?

00:07:57.434 --> 00:07:59.501
I mean, if you've ever been
cheated by a dog,

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:05.167
that's the definition of
a "shame on you" situation.

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:09.734
Did a dog once pretend to throw
a tennis ball to Trump?

00:08:09.734 --> 00:08:12.300
[As Trump] "I once met
this dog -- big dog, strong dog.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.834
And he said to me,
'Do you want the ball?'

00:08:13.834 --> 00:08:16.534
And I did. I did want the ball.

00:08:16.534 --> 00:08:17.701
And he knew I wanted the ball

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:19.267
because I was doing
a little dance.

00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:21.300
And so -- and so he threw it,

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:26.334
but little -- little did I know,
it was only a pretend throw.

00:08:26.334 --> 00:08:27.734
It was a fake-out throw

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:30.100
and he kept it in his paw,
hidden behind his back.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:31.434
But I was looking everywhere.

00:08:31.434 --> 00:08:34.601
I was...looking for the ball
under the couch,

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:37.634
behind the --
getting more agitated

00:08:37.634 --> 00:08:40.767
with every passing second,
so badly did I want that ball.

00:08:40.767 --> 00:08:43.934
I wanted it, so I was
spinning myself in circles.

00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:45.667
The whole thing was very,
very unfair.

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:48.567
No one's been treated worse
by a dog than I have.

00:08:48.567 --> 00:08:49.968
In the history of America,

00:08:49.968 --> 00:08:52.667
no one's ever been treated worse
than I have --

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:57.200
you know, and the worst people,
the worst people are dogs."

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.567
[Normally] So now,
instead of just claiming

00:08:58.567 --> 00:09:00.801
the 2020 presidential election
was rigged against him,

00:09:00.801 --> 00:09:02.968
Trump is going a step further
and claiming in advance

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:04.467
that all elections are rigged.

00:09:04.467 --> 00:09:06.567
We can't have a functioning
democracy where one side

00:09:06.567 --> 00:09:10.167
just insists that every time
they lose, it's illegitimate

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:12.667
and that they're the only ones
entitled to hold power.

00:09:12.667 --> 00:09:14.200
I mean, you don't see
Mets fans insisting

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.534
they actually won the division

00:09:15.534 --> 00:09:17.133
after getting swept
by the Braves this week.

00:09:17.133 --> 00:09:18.801
And they're accepting defeat
the way they always have --

00:09:18.801 --> 00:09:20.734
by being absolutely [bleep]
miserable, you know?

00:09:20.734 --> 00:09:22.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.667 --> 00:09:24.100
That's how democracy
is supposed to work.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.400
The winners celebrate
and the losers

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.267
sit at home crying
into their Jacob deGrom jersey.

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.868
And by the way, lest you think
I'm picking on the Mets,

00:09:29.868 --> 00:09:33.801
I'm a Steelers fan and we lost
to the Jets this weekend.

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:37.133
Yeah, the Jet-- those Jets.

00:09:37.133 --> 00:09:38.801
I went to the game,
and you know what the worst part

00:09:38.801 --> 00:09:40.234
about flying
from New York to Pittsburgh

00:09:40.234 --> 00:09:41.734
to watch your beloved Steelers
lose is?

00:09:41.734 --> 00:09:46.834
Flying home on a plane full of
[bleep] Jets fans all drinking

00:09:46.834 --> 00:09:49.834
and partying like
they just won the Super Bowl.

00:09:49.834 --> 00:09:51.234
And hey, again,
if you're a Jets fan,

00:09:51.234 --> 00:09:55.734
being 2-2 in October,
that's your Super Bowl.

00:09:55.734 --> 00:09:58.734
Enjoy it while it lasts.

00:09:58.734 --> 00:10:00.801
Traffic was so bad today with
the [bleep] parade

00:10:00.801 --> 00:10:02.133
on Fifth Avenue.

00:10:02.133 --> 00:10:05.033
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.033 --> 00:10:06.634
Tickertape.

00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:10.300
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.567
The point is, the GOP does not
have a discernible ideology

00:10:13.567 --> 00:10:14.734
that's separate from Trumpism.

00:10:14.734 --> 00:10:16.767
In fact, they've had
ample opportunity

00:10:16.767 --> 00:10:18.334
to separate themselves
from Trump over the years.

00:10:18.334 --> 00:10:20.501
And even now,
after he's been rejected

00:10:20.501 --> 00:10:22.567
over and over by voters
and remains under multiple

00:10:22.567 --> 00:10:23.834
serious criminal investigations,

00:10:23.834 --> 00:10:25.434
they refuse to denounce him.
Over the weekend,

00:10:25.434 --> 00:10:28.067
Trump even attacked
their own Senate leader,

00:10:28.067 --> 00:10:30.100
Mitch McConnell,
and McConnell's wife,

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:31.868
former Transportation Secretary
Elaine Chao.

00:10:31.868 --> 00:10:34.567
And even then,
Florida Senator Rick Scott

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:36.234
still could not find it
within him

00:10:36.234 --> 00:10:38.501
to stand up for his Senate
colleague and denounce Trump.

00:10:38.501 --> 00:10:42.200
-I have to ask you about
what appears to be a threat

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.601
by former President Trump
against your colleague,

00:10:45.601 --> 00:10:48.701
Senate Republican leader
Mitch McConnell.

00:10:48.701 --> 00:10:50.801
Trump said, quote,
"He has a death wish"

00:10:50.801 --> 00:10:53.200
for supporting Democratic
sponsored bills.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.601
He also mocked McConnell's wife

00:10:55.601 --> 00:10:57.767
and his own former
Transportation Secretary,

00:10:57.767 --> 00:11:00.300
Elaine Chao, as, quote,
"China-loving."

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.033
And "Coco Chow."

00:11:02.033 --> 00:11:04.734
You're a member
of the Senate GOP leadership.

00:11:04.734 --> 00:11:06.334
Are you okay with this?

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:11.634
-Well, look, I can
never talk about --

00:11:11.634 --> 00:11:13.534
respond to why anybody else
says what they said,

00:11:13.534 --> 00:11:15.767
but here's what -- is the way
I looked at it,

00:11:15.767 --> 00:11:19.167
is I think, you know,
what the president is saying is,

00:11:19.167 --> 00:11:21.133
you know, we've -- there's been
a lot of money

00:11:21.133 --> 00:11:23.267
spent over the last two years.

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:25.601
We've got to make sure we don't
keep caving to Democrats.

00:11:25.601 --> 00:11:27.033
It's causing
unbelievable inflation

00:11:27.033 --> 00:11:30.267
and causing more and more debt.
As you know, you know,

00:11:30.267 --> 00:11:32.601
the president
likes to give people nicknames

00:11:32.601 --> 00:11:35.767
so you can ask him how
he came up with the nickname.

00:11:35.767 --> 00:11:37.467
I'm sure he has
a nickname for me.

00:11:37.467 --> 00:11:41.400
-First of all, he definitely
has a nickname for you.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.200
Trump wouldn't ever even try
to rhyme or be alliterative.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:47.901
[As Trump] We all know
Penis Rick.

00:11:47.901 --> 00:11:49.501
He tries to wear a hat to
confuse us,

00:11:49.501 --> 00:11:50.667
but we know what he looks like.

00:11:50.667 --> 00:11:54.167
If only there was a word that
rhymed with Rick

00:11:54.167 --> 00:11:55.400
that also meant penis.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:11:58.667 --> 00:12:00.067
[Normally] I think the most
insulting part

00:12:00.067 --> 00:12:01.467
of these interviews
is always when they try

00:12:01.467 --> 00:12:03.100
to explain away something
that was very clearly

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.601
a deranged outburst from Trump
as if it was something

00:12:05.601 --> 00:12:07.567
that was a sophisticated
take on politics.

00:12:07.567 --> 00:12:09.701
"Dana, what I think
the president was saying

00:12:09.701 --> 00:12:12.601
is that we have to encourage
people to consume more,

00:12:12.601 --> 00:12:14.267
which will in turn
drive up supply,

00:12:14.267 --> 00:12:15.767
thus boosting the economy."

00:12:15.767 --> 00:12:18.133
"Senator, he tweeted,
'Eat my nuts.'"

00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:20.534
"Yes.

00:12:20.534 --> 00:12:23.000
You see, Dana,
he wants us to consume

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.234
more almonds and cashews to
promote American agriculture."

00:12:27.234 --> 00:12:30.100
"Well, Senator, his next Tweet
was, 'And when I say nuts,

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.100
I don't mean almonds
and cashews.'"

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.601
"Again, Dana, maybe he meant
peanuts or macadamia nuts.

00:12:35.601 --> 00:12:37.133
We could go back
and forth all day

00:12:37.133 --> 00:12:39.334
trying to put ourselves
in his head, and I don't know."

00:12:39.334 --> 00:12:41.767
"His next Tweet was,
'I mean testicles.'"

00:12:41.767 --> 00:12:43.601
"I think --
I think I'm going to go, Dana."

00:12:43.601 --> 00:12:45.901
"Thank you for joining us,
Senator Penis Rick."

00:12:45.901 --> 00:12:48.400
With midterms approaching
and the polls tight,

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.968
Republicans want to pretend
they have a serious

00:12:49.968 --> 00:12:52.033
governing platform,
but Trump makes that impossible

00:12:52.033 --> 00:12:53.868
because he constantly
rips the mask off,

00:12:53.868 --> 00:12:55.267
revealing that they are,
in fact,

00:12:55.267 --> 00:12:56.467
not a serious governing party.

00:12:56.467 --> 00:12:58.601
They're entirely
devoted to the cult of Trumpism

00:12:58.601 --> 00:13:01.100
and the threat
he poses to democracy.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.100
They're all his friends,
his loyal servants,

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:05.467
his closest allies,
or as Trump himself may put it,

00:13:05.467 --> 00:13:07.634
they're all his...
-Dogs.

00:13:07.634 --> 00:13:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:13:08.634 --> 00:13:11.067
-[Mocking] "Dogs."

00:13:11.067 --> 00:13:12.667
[Normally] This has been
A Closer Look.

00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:15.901
♪♪

00:13:15.901 --> 00:13:17.601
The midterm elections
are coming up,

00:13:17.601 --> 00:13:20.534
so to make sure that you're good
to vote in this election,

00:13:20.534 --> 00:13:23.367
visit our good friends
at HeadCount.org

00:13:23.367 --> 00:13:25.501
to check
your voter registration status

00:13:25.501 --> 00:13:27.300
or to register to vote.

